      "title": "Office365 category email summary",
      "subtitle": "",
      "status": "Draft",
      "notes": "# Result Summary\n- Outlook category: `CanDoItAllSummaryTest`\n- Message count: 1\n- Outcome: summarized customer request for a Tetris game project\n\n# Evidence Table\n| Source | Sender | Subject | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Outlook message `AAMkAGRmMWViOTA2LTMzNGItNGNjNi1hMThmLWY2ZjA2ZTA1NjU4NwBGAAAAAABzw7m6jM_ATK0mFMmFWzQABwCKp9BRbAdVSoi7nuYgsTwNAAAAAAEMAACKp9BRbAdVSoi7nuYgsTwNAAUlI8yQAAA=` | tomas.svo1@gmail.com | Tetris Game Development | \"We need to program a simple Tetris game\"; \"in the form of a website\"; \"mobile application ... later\"; \"controlled with the keyboard\"; \"save the last maximum score\"; \"no backend\"; \"host it on a regular static web hosting\"; \"within one week\" |\n\n# Concrete Findings\n- Primary request is a browser-based Tetris game.\n- Mobile app is optional/later, not the immediate requirement.\n- Controls must support keyboard input, including arrows or WASD.\n- Score persistence must be local to the app; no backend is wanted.\n- Delivery target is one week.\n\n# Open Gaps\n- No detailed functional spec for scoring, levels, pause/restart, or game-over behavior.\n- No design requirements, brand assets, or acceptance criteria were provided.\n- No mobile scope details beyond a possible future request.\n\n# Recommended Next Actions\n1. Confirm the exact website scope and minimum viable feature set.\n2. Define technical approach for static hosting and local score storage.\n3. Estimate delivery for the one-week deadline.\n4. Ask whether the mobile app should be treated as a separate phase or backlog item.",
